; Triangular_ZigZag_Largest5_5mms_Flow1p4
; Bambu Lab P1S / 0.2 mm nozzle / PETG; TRIANGULAR zigzags, not square waves
; 5 specimens, each a mirrored pair; 10 layers at 0.06 mm (0.60 mm total)
; Largest 5 distinct original triangle tip spacings: 0.6, 0.7, 0.8, 0.9, 1.0 mm
; All model layers 5 mm/s; XY nozzle-load/purge line 20 mm/s
; Reference: FZigZagSquare1.4.gcode; nozzle 255 C; bed 70 C; M900 K0.55 L1000 M10
; Part fan off layers 1-3, PWM229 (~90%) layers 4-10; auxiliary fan off during model
; First-layer acceleration 500; upper-layer acceleration 2000 mm/s^2
; Commanded width 0.162876 mm (reference's dominant width); flow ratio 1.4; filament diameter 1.75 mm
; E per path mm = 0.005238467421; flow is baked into E, not applied again with M221
; Exact original triangle vertices retained within 0.00001 mm; collinear sampling removed
; 10 mm straight intro/outro on every path; retract 0.4 mm over 2 mm wipe, then lift
; Complete each mirrored pair before moving left to right to the next specimen
; Static validation only; this new triangular print has not been physically verified
; EXECUTABLE_BLOCK_START
M201 X20000 Y20000 Z500 E5000
M203 X500 Y500 Z20 E30
M204 P20000 R5000 T20000
M205 X9.00 Y9.00 Z3.00 E2.50 ; sets the jerk limits, mm/sec
M106 S0
M106 P2 S0
